# WHAT IT COVERS: the second 2026-10-26 stream, 43.7 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows,
# captured through NvFBC with o:vsync: a synthesized present is drawn by the optical flow warp, or
# by the blend when the flow was planned too late or not at all. That changes how a synthesized
# present looks and nothing the replay models; the policy is the one the tree ships. The first
# o:vsync stream here. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 473 times (650 an hour) and stalled for
# 100 ms or more 107 times (147 an hour), in 86 bursts, 55 of them with a stall, and with no
# periodic stretch; the last 3.5 minutes (2444 s to 2650 s) are the dice game, dense 51 to 60 ms
# hitches with no stall. The lock released 3 times in the field, at 754.43, 1331.18 and 1713.05
# s; the replay releases at the same three moments and once more, at 1686.35 s. The worst blend
# run is 17 presents in the field and on the replay, where it sits at 1182.58 s. Of the 19 moves
# on the replay, 8 of them late, 2 land more than 2 ms from a real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 49.466 s, from the 2470
# marked frames in its first 41 s, 2468 of them on time within 0.39 ms of that offset (p90); the
# other 2 the card or OBS showed a refresh late. The video runs 2620.6 s with no holes, opens on
# gameplay in the forest (a few seconds of the map and one black frame, all marked) and ends on
# gameplay at the dice game and the tavern table, so the cut is the whole video, 49.5 s to 2670.1 s
# of log time, and the marked frames lie inside it. Inside the cut, 36 seconds in 35 runs fall
# out of the 60 fps regime, each a single hitch second or two in a row.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay line reads synth 1.3% against 1.3%, worst run 17 against 17, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and
# pull wraps 77 against 77. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran, blends are 1983
# against 1969, repeats 851 against 851, skips 296 against 296, pull wraps 105.9 an hour against
# 105.8 and the worst run 17 against 17. The replay makes 19 moves and the field's log has 20 in
# the window; the three field releases match within 0.42 ms, and the replay releases once more,
# at 1686.35 s, where the field kept the lock.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
